nvgpu: trace the GPU's power-on (diagnostic, not applied)

For trials 7 and 8. Trial 6's 5.10 boot stopped completing SD card I/O
right when nvgpu first powered the GPU. This prints who started the
power-on, each init step before it runs, the rail gating, the first DVFS
voltage requests and the result of each gm20b clock step. It changes no
behaviour.

Trial 7's last logged step was init_clk_support, which led to 0007.
Applied in trials 7 to 24; set aside for trial 25. The other patches apply
without it.

Licence: GPL-2.0-only. Lab notes, with every measurement: NOTES.md.
---
diff --git a/nvidia/drivers/soc/tegra/tegra-dvfs.c b/nvidia/drivers/soc/tegra/tegra-dvfs.c
index 9c892a43b..1b88366aa 100644
--- a/nvidia/drivers/soc/tegra/tegra-dvfs.c
+++ b/nvidia/drivers/soc/tegra/tegra-dvfs.c
@@ -174,8 +174,14 @@ static void dvfs_rail_stats_update(
 
 static int dvfs_rail_set_voltage_reg(struct dvfs_rail *rail, int millivolts)
 {
+	static unsigned int traced;
 	int ret;
 
+	if (traced < 200) {
+		traced++;
+		pr_info("tegra_dvfs: %s to %d mV\n", rail->reg_id, millivolts);
+	}
+
 	if (rail->joint_rail_with_dfll)
 		tegra_dfll_set_external_floor_mv(rail->new_millivolts);
 
@@ -1657,6 +1663,7 @@ int tegra_dvfs_rail_power_up(struct dvfs_rail *rail)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
 	mutex_lock(&dvfs_lock);
+	pr_info("tegra_dvfs: %s power up\n", rail->reg_id);
 	if (rail->reg) {
 		ret = regulator_enable(rail->reg);
 		if (!ret && !timekeeping_suspended) {
@@ -1678,6 +1685,7 @@ int tegra_dvfs_rail_power_down(struct dvfs_rail *rail)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
 	mutex_lock(&dvfs_lock);
+	pr_info("tegra_dvfs: %s power down\n", rail->reg_id);
 	if (rail->reg) {
 		ret = regulator_disable(rail->reg);
 		if (!ret && !timekeeping_suspended) {
